WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.661
This is a week with Mr R Science:

00:00:02.661 --> 00:00:06.000
what Mr Robert's pupils do after a lesson, and why.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.298
Every lesson starts with a few quick questions on earlier work.

00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:13.835
No notes, no hints.

00:00:13.835 --> 00:00:14.240
Just:

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.292
did it stick?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.531
In class, Mr Robert teaches from the coursebook.

00:00:19.531 --> 00:00:23.840
The live lab runs on the TV, and pupils write in their own book.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.168
That evening, pupils watch one short lesson in his own voice.

00:00:29.168 --> 00:00:31.646
It stops, and asks them to predict.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.568
Mr Robert:

00:00:32.568 --> 00:00:33.903
"Your turn to think.

00:00:33.903 --> 00:00:36.374
The salt bridge is potassium nitrate.

00:00:36.374 --> 00:00:40.246
Which ions move out of the bridge into the zinc half-cell?

00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:42.650
Pause the lesson and write it down."

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.498
They have to think before he explains.

00:00:46.498 --> 00:00:47.613
Then they train.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:52.422
Fresh numbers every time, and a hint only opens after a real attempt.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.842
Then it's back to paper:

00:00:54.842 --> 00:00:58.206
the matching exercise in pen, marked from the answer book.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.082
At the end of the week, three fresh questions with the help switched off.

00:01:04.082 --> 00:01:06.660
Then the weekly task that Mr Robert marks.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.170
And a few days later, it comes back.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.464
Three quick questions, to check it really stuck.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.731
Watch, train, write, check.

00:01:16.731 --> 00:01:19.719
About half an hour after each lesson.

00:01:19.719 --> 00:01:24.322
It's free, there's no sign-in, and it works on any phone.
